DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20261210T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20261210T194500
SUMMARY:Nutcracker: Cast B Dress Rehearsal – ACT I Cast B (Mandatory 
 – Production Week)
LOCATION:Robinson Center
DESCRIPTION:*** THIS DAY ***\nCALL TIME 6:00 PM — be checked in and bac
 kstage by then. ARRIVE BY 5:45 PM.\nOn stage: 7:00 PM–7:45 PM.\nACT I 
 Dress Run\; In Performance Costumes\, Hair and Makeup.\nMANDATORY — pr
 oduction week.\n\n*** STANDING RULES ***\nBA: Call Time is the time danc
 ers should be check-in and backstage - Arrive 15 minutes before Call Tim
 e.\nBA: Mandatory Rehearsals (1st Rehearsal\, Rehearsals after Thanksgiv
 ing and Production Week Rehearsals and Performances).\nAll Casts are cal
 led unless a cast is named.\nSUBJECT TO CHANGE — the BA master schedul
 e\, the weekly BA emails and the BA portal are the official source. Mast
 er: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1xWFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-N
 7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\n*** COSTUME / HAIR / MAKEUP — Snow ***\nSnow — C
 ostume (you provide): Pink Seamless Tights\, Pink Bloomers\; Shoes: Pink
  Pointe Shoes w/ ribbons & elastics (clean\, quiet\, unpancacked)\; Make
 up: Full Stage Makeup\; Hair: French Twist\; Accessories (BA provides): 
 Headpiece\nFull Stage Makeup Instruction Sheet:\n• Apply foundation an
 d powder matching skintone\n• Light skin tone eye shadow over entire e
 ye\n• Dark brown eye shadow over crease\n• Medium brown eye shadow b
 lended over brown\n• Black fake eyelashes (note: apply mascara to own 
 lashes before application of fake lashes)\n• Apply eyeliner after lash
 es dry\n• Blush on the cheeks (be sure to apply plenty so dancer doesn
 ’t look washed out in the stage lights)\n• Brown or tan on contour c
 heekbones\, hairline\n• Use a brow pencil (or eyeshadow) to darken the
  eyebrows\n• Red or Dark Red Lipstick\nDancers of Color may wear flesh
  tone tights and flesh tone ballet shoes.\nCostume Care Guidelines:\n•
  Handle costume pieces with care while changing to prevent damage to del
 icate fabrics\n• Promptly notify Ballet Arkansas in the event of costu
 me damage at the point of discovery\, no matter how significant\n• Nev
 er throw costumes or accessories on the floor\, or hang costumes by thei
 r elastic straps\n• Refrain from sitting on the floor while in costume
 \n• Do not attempt to alter\, mend\, clean\, or launder any costume or
  accessory\n• Never apply stage make-up while in costume and shall tak
 e great care to refrain from smudging make-up on costume during its remo
 val\n• Refrain from the use of spray perfume or cologne while in costu
 me\n• Never wear any garment not assigned to cast member\n• Do not h
 andle or consume food or beverage while in costume\, with the exception 
 of water\n• Do not remove costumes from their assigned dressing rooms 
 or from the theater\n• Remove all bobby pins used to secure head piece
 s and wigs following their use\n• Return all headpieces to their assig
 ned bags\n• Comply fully with any and all updates to Ballet Arkansas
 ’ wardrobe policies\n• Do not pack markers\, paints\, colored drinks
  or anything that may damage or stain costumes.
